<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the app target.

  One key, and it is not optional: without `aps-environment`,
  `registerForRemoteNotifications()` fails on a real device and no push token is
  ever issued. The app would look like it worked -- it asks for notification
  permission, the operator says yes, nothing ever arrives -- which is the worst
  shape a failure can have.

  `development` here is what Xcode substitutes for a Debug build; a Release
  archive built for the App Store gets `production` from the profile it is signed
  with. That switch is exactly why the relay needs to be told which APNs
  environment it is talking to (see `docs/relay-deployment.md` §10.2): a token
  from one is refused by the other, with an error that names neither.

  Enabling the capability is also required on the App ID itself -- either in the
  developer portal, or by adding "Push Notifications" under Signing &
  Capabilities in Xcode with automatic signing on. See `docs/testflight.md`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
